    "body": "## Motivation\n\nGemma 3 and Gemma 4 fail to start with `--lora-target-modules all`:\n\n```text\nAttributeError: 'Gemma3TextScaledWordEmbedding' object has no attribute 'org_vocab_size'\n```\n\n`all` unconditionally adds `embed_tokens` and `lm_head`, even when auto-detection excludes them. Gemma uses a scaled `nn.Embedding` that the embedding LoRA wrapper does not support. Since `lm_head` shares that embedding, adding it as a target triggers conversion to `ParallelLMHead`, which reads the missing `org_vocab_size` attribute.\n\n## Modifications\n\nOnly add both embedding targets when auto-detection finds a `VocabParallelEmbedding` or `ParallelLMHead`. Supported parallel embeddings keep the same targets, including a tied `lm_head`.\n\nFor Gemma, `all` selects the supported projections and skips the tied-head conversion. The original embedding, its scaling, and the shared output weights remain in use. No embedding LoRA wrappers are installed; existing checks already skip their LoRA buffer allocation and updates.\n\nThis fixes startup for projection-only adapters; it does not add Gemma embedding LoRA support. With `all`, an adapter that explicitly lists `embed_tokens` or `lm_head` is rejected by the existing target validation.\n\nAdd two regression tests: a tied parallel embedding still gets both targets, and a tied plain `nn.Embedding` gets neither.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nReproduced on `797af71`, one L4, with no adapter loaded:\n\n```bash\npython -m sglang.launch_server --model-path unsloth/gemma-3-1b-it \\\n  --enable-lora --lora-target-modules all --max-lora-rank 8 \\\n  --attention-backend triton --disable-cuda-graph --mem-fraction-static 0.5\n```\n\nWith the fix, the server starts and serves requests both with and without a rank-8 `all-linear` adapter. A tiny Gemma 4 checkpoint reproduces the same embedding error before the fix.\n\nOriginal CPU validation (PyTorch 2.14.1, Transformers 5.19.0): **33 passed** across the four LoRA unit-test files. The plain-embedding regression fails without the fix; the tied-parallel-embedding test passes before and after.\n\nPre-commit passes on `c8704818`.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A. This changes startup target selection.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format with pre-commit.\n- [x] Add regression tests.\n- [ ] Update documentation (not needed).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41585303413](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41585303413)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41585303388](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41585303388)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41585303245](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41585303245)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
